From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] input: rsinput: the MCU scan fields as parameters

The params command carries two big-endian 32-bit fields, 0x28 and
0x07, neither of which the driver explained. Reading the MCU's own
firmware out of the stock Android install settles both: the handler
logs them itself as

    E:%s(%d) debounce %d frame_rate %d

and they are a joystick deadband and the delay between scans.

debounce, 40, is a deadband in raw ADC counts, not a time. Every read
site compares |sample - previous| against it and keeps the old value
below the threshold. At the +-1024 range this device's DT sets, 40
counts is about 2% of half travel.

frame_rate, 7, is a wait at the end of each scan pass, in SysTick
ticks. SysTick reloads at SystemCoreClock/10000 - 1, so a tick is
100 us and the vendor value is 0.7 ms. Below 1 the wait is skipped
entirely. That is 8% of the measured 9.0 ms period; the rest is
bit-banged I2C to the two Hall sensors, ten register reads a pass,
with no I2C peripheral involved at all.

Both default to the vendor values. frame_rate=0 is the experiment
worth running: it should take the median report interval from 9.0 ms
to about 8.3 ms and no further. If it moves by that much, the tick
unit and the scan model are confirmed; if it does not move, the
reading is wrong and nothing further should be built on it. #447.

Parameters rather than constants because the meaning of both fields
is inferred from firmware nobody documented, and because a pad that
misbehaves is recovered with rsinput.frame_rate=7 on the cmdline
rather than a reflash.

--- a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
@@ -55,6 +55,31 @@
 static int axis_righty_max=0x580;
 static int axis_righty_deadzone=0x0;
 static int axis_righty_antideadzone=0x0;
+
+/*
+ * The two fields of the MCU params command, named by the MCU
+ * firmware's own log line: "debounce %d frame_rate %d".
+ *
+ * stick_deadband is in raw ADC counts. The MCU keeps the previous
+ * sample unless |new - old| exceeds it, so it is hysteresis on the
+ * axis, not a time. 40 is the vendor value, about 2% of half travel
+ * at +-1024.
+ *
+ * frame_rate is the wait at the end of each scan pass, in 100 us
+ * SysTick ticks, and the MCU skips it entirely below 1. The vendor's
+ * 7 is 0.7 ms of the 9.0 ms measured period; the remainder is
+ * bit-banged I2C to the Hall sensors and is not reachable from here.
+ */
+static int stick_deadband = 40;
+static int frame_rate = 7;
+
+module_param(stick_deadband,int,0660);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(stick_deadband,
+    "MCU joystick deadband in ADC counts (vendor default 40)");
+
+module_param(frame_rate,int,0660);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(frame_rate,
+    "MCU scan delay in 100us ticks, 0 disables (vendor default 7)");
 
 module_param(update_params,int,0660);
 
@@ -238,10 +270,18 @@
 static int rsinput_init_commands(struct rsinput_driver *drv) {
     static const uint8_t version_request[] = {DATA_COMMOD_VERSION};
-    static const uint8_t mcu_params[] = {
-        DATA_COMMOD_SET_PAR,
-        0x01,
-        0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x28,
-        0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x07
-    };
+    /* Built per call, not static: both fields come from module
+     * parameters that are writable at runtime. */
+    const uint8_t mcu_params[] = {
+        DATA_COMMOD_SET_PAR,
+        0x01,
+        (stick_deadband >> 24) & 0xff,
+        (stick_deadband >> 16) & 0xff,
+        (stick_deadband >>  8) & 0xff,
+         stick_deadband        & 0xff,
+        (frame_rate >> 24) & 0xff,
+        (frame_rate >> 16) & 0xff,
+        (frame_rate >>  8) & 0xff,
+         frame_rate        & 0xff
+    };
     unsigned long timeout = msecs_to_jiffies(MCU_VERSION_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS);
